        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en"># Included processes\nWind turbine substructure (including transition piece), at site including manufacturing, transports, installation, replacements, decommission and waste treatement. Calculated for FU of 1p.\nData of material inputs are based on the offshore wind turbine REpower 5M, with a nominal capacity of 5 MW, as used in the Ormonde offshore wind farm, UK.\nThe modelled substructure represents a jacket foundation including piles, lattice and transition piece.\nThe distance to installation port is assumed to be 187 km. The average water depth is 19 m. \nAssumed lifetime is 25 years.\n\nMain data source regarding material composition: \nKouloumpis, V., &amp; Azapagic, A. (2022). A model for estimating life cycle environmental impacts of offshore wind electricity considering specific characteristics of wind farms. Sustainable Production and Consumption, 29, 495–506. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.spc.2021.10.024</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
        </technology>
    </processInformation>
